- Probability of delay.
- Feature importance where supported.
- Confusion matrix.
- Accuracy.
- Precision.
- Recall.
- F1-score.
- ROC-AUC where applicable.

Compare ensemble performance with individual classification algorithms.

Identify the best-performing model using actual evaluation results.

Do not automatically declare an ensemble model as the winner.

The best model should be selected using a clearly stated evaluation criterion, preferably F1-score and ROC-AUC, while considering precision and recall.

