# 14. IMPORTANT MACHINE LEARNING REQUIREMENTS

These requirements are mandatory:

1. Every specified ML algorithm must be implemented, not merely displayed as a name in the interface.
2. Models must use actual training and testing data.
3. Use consistent feature engineering and appropriate preprocessing.
4. Avoid data leakage.
5. Do not hardcode accuracy, precision, recall, F1-score or other evaluation metrics.
6. Regression and classification must be treated as different prediction tasks.
7. Clustering must be evaluated using suitable clustering metrics.
8. All classification models must be evaluated on a comparable test dataset.
9. Use actual model outputs for prediction visualizations.
10. Save trained models where appropriate.
11. Support retraining when a new dataset is uploaded.
12. Display warnings when insufficient data is available.
13. Clearly distinguish synthetic sample data from real-world data.
14. Handle class imbalance where necessary.
15. Provide meaningful explanations for predictions.

For classification, use suitable metrics including Accuracy, Precision, Recall, F1-score, ROC-AUC and Confusion Matrix.

For regression, use MAE, MSE, RMSE and R².

For clustering, use Silhouette Score and appropriate cluster visualizations.

Do not force every algorithm into every task. Use each algorithm for the problem it is designed to solve.

